# Psych Engine externs for the Haxe -> Lua shim

`:psych_externs` describes the *outside world* that Psych's `source/psychlua/*.hx`
talks to. Nothing here is an implementation: every class maps to something Light
Engine already owns (camera, sprites, conductor, paths), so compiling Psych's own
Lua layer produces code that calls into this engine.

Everything is `extern`, so Haxe only type-checks against it and emits calls to
the matching Lua globals. The Lua side is installed by
`funkin/backend/scripts/psych/bridge.lua`.

Inventory derived from Psych 1.0.4 `source/psychlua/*.hx`:
  Paths            16 static members
  LuaUtils         22 static members
  FlxG             12 static members
  PlayState         8 static members
  plus Conductor, Mods, ClientPrefs, MusicBeatState, FlxTransitionableState,
  Song, Note, Assets, FlxColor, FlxEase, FlxTween and the constructors
  FlxText/FlxSprite/FlxSound/FlxTimer/FlxSave.
